WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.530
Build a small evaluation set from the intended workload.

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:06.660
Include common prompts, difficult edge cases, required formats,

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.843
representative context lengths, and tasks with verifiable outcomes.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:13.190
Keep the base model, runtime, prompt template, sampling settings,

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.150
and hardware constant while comparing quantization variants.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.335
Otherwise, the test cannot isolate precision as the changed variable.

00:00:19.335 --> 00:00:22.700
Compare at least one compact candidate, one practical middle candidate,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.345
and a higher-precision reference when hardware allows.

00:00:25.345 --> 00:00:29.580
Measure file size, loaded VRAM or RAM, model load time, time to first token,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.940
prompt-processing speed, generation speed, power or temperature if relevant, and errors.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.220
Run multiple trials so warm caches and random output do not determine the result.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.460
Score quality against predefined criteria.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.740
For coding, run tests.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.375
For extraction, compare fields.

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:45.475
For structured output, validate the format.

00:00:45.475 --> 00:00:47.940
For analysis, review correctness and consistency.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.945
Long-context evaluation should use material that requires retrieval from different

00:00:51.945 --> 00:00:52.417
positions.

00:00:52.417 --> 00:00:54.615
Record failures, not only average impressions,

00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:58.500
because one serious instruction-following defect may outweigh a small speed gain.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.950
Keep a concise decision log with model revision, quantization file, runtime version,

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.455
settings, hardware, measurements, and acceptance result.

00:01:05.455 --> 00:01:09.540
Select the lowest-resource option that meets quality and reliability requirements with

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.380
memory headroom.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.540
Revisit the decision when the model, runtime, hardware, or workload changes.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.460
Testing turns quantization from a label into an evidence-based deployment choice.
